+## Prefer the persistent source-run coordinator
+
+For supported complete sources, use `experimental-source-run` to manage the
+ordered bindings and saved baselines rather than rebuilding an operation map by
+hand. All actions take SOURCE, `--run-state RUN.json`, exact `--did/--wid/--eid`,
+`--bridge-config CONFIG`, `--journal JOURNAL`, and `--tab-id TAB`.
+
+1. `init` validates the complete source locally and pins its hash, semantics,
+   target and journal. Resume the existing run after interruption; never create
+   a new run to bypass observed features or an unresolved operation.
+2. `next` verifies saved idle state and returns `browser_allocate`, with exact
+   source references and required native defaults. Allocate only that blank
+   feature using normal Browser controls. Do not draw source geometry manually.
+3. `apply` validates the fresh draft against its saved baseline, populates it
+   using the existing guarded writers, and adopts only independently observed
+   journal results. Repeat from `next`. Do not replay an uncertain operation.
+4. Final `verify_geometry` means feature definitions are saved, not automatically
+   proven solids. Measure solid count, volume, area and bounds independently;
+   edit and restore a native variable and compare identities and definitions.
+
+The companion must report its loaded creation target, matching the private config
+and requested target. `doctor --bridge-config CONFIG` reports this target.
+Editing the config alone does not retarget the running companion. A target change
+requires the coordinated companion restart after saved idle/clear journal checks.
+
+Explicit REMOVE additionally requires both `h2_source_remove_server_v1` and
+`h2_source_remove_page_v1`. The coordinator returns a separate
+`target_body_reference` bound to a previously observed NEW extrusion from a single
+rectangle or circle. Choose SOLID/REMOVE/BLIND, whole source sketch, forward
+direction (`oppositeDirection: false`), and only the indicated body with
+`defaultScope: false`. Selecting REMOVE may automatically reverse direction in
+Onshape; check it before applying. Multiple-body targets and a second cut of an
+already-cut body are not supported by the coordinator. Do not bypass these limits
+using direct commands. Native query lineage and complete current body scope need
+separate proof before expanding that support.
+
+After Browser measurements, optional `record-measurements --measurements FILE.json`
+records caller-supplied totals and screenshot hashes against the current revision.
+The JSON contains `target`, `source_sha256`, `revision`,
+`method: "browser_mass_properties"`, integer `parts`, positive `volume_mm3` and
+`area_mm2`, and `screenshots` (PNG/JPEG paths relative to the JSON). Counts must
+match the local model; volume/area tolerance is 0.002 absolute or 1e-7 relative.
+This comparison does not read pixels or acquire measurements automatically:
+`geometry_verified` remains false. Later `next` calls flag a stale revision or
+changed/missing evidence. Retain the independent geometric and editability report.
+
